The conjecture claims parse_content returns the same verdict for the reply texts "3.14" and "{}". Under the documented rule, "3.14" should be INVALID_JSON because no object is recovered and no refusal phrase is present, while "{}" should be JSON_OBJECT because an object is recovered. The function, however, first tries loads_strict(content) and returns JSON_OBJECT on any successful strict parse, so it returns JSON_OBJECT for both. The author would be wrong if parse_content returns INVALID_JSON for "3.14" (e.g., if loads_strict rejects non-object JSON values or if recover_json_object is consulted before the verdict is set).